course: dictionary
lesson: 11353
title: The zither: a plucked string instrument
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A zither is a musical instrument with many strings stretched over a flat wooden box. You lay it on a table or on your lap, then pluck the strings with your fingers or a pick. Zither is a noun, so it names a thing: one zither, two zithers.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence: «The guzheng is a Chinese plucked zither with strings over movable bridges.» Plucked tells you the strings are pulled, not blown or hit. The guzheng is called a zither, so it is a kind of zither. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? An instrument with strings.
explain: Zithers belong to the string family because the sound comes from strings that vibrate when you pluck them. In Austria and Germany, zithers are often played in folk music. You can play the zither, or listen to zither music.
fact: A zither is a musical instrument with many strings.
fact: The strings are stretched over a flat wooden box.
fact: You pluck the strings with your fingers or a pick.
fact: The guzheng, the koto and the kantele are related zithers.
fact: Zithers belong to the string family because their sound comes from vibrating strings.
exercise: «The guzheng is a Chinese plucked zither with strings over movable bridges.» What kind of instrument is a guzheng? | A flute | *A zither | A drum | A trumpet
exercise: How do you play a zither? | Blow into it like a whistle | *Pluck the strings with your fingers or a pick | Hit the wooden box with a stick | Shake it hard to make it ring
exercise: Which family of instruments does the zither belong to? | *Strings | Percussion | Brass | Woodwind
test: In which countries is the zither played in folk music? | Finland and Sweden | Japan and China | *Austria and Germany | Spain and Italy
test: Which phrase means playing the instrument? | Zither box | Zither music | Flat wooden zither | *Play the zither
exam: What is a zither's strings stretched over? | A metal tube | A stone | A glass bowl | *A flat wooden box
